WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.943 --> 00:00:01.776
(gentle music)

00:00:01.776 --> 00:00:03.700
- [Narrator] How is it doing that?

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:07.220
Hamsters, like Soda
Pop, can stuff up to 20%

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:10.430
of their body weight into their cheeks.

00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:13.300
For comparison, that's
like the average person

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:16.690
carrying around 30 extra pounds of food,

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:20.270
or about 120 quarter pounders.

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:23.960
It would be a cool party
trick, but not very comfortable

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:26.820
or, let's face it, even possible.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:29.600
That's where hamsters are different.

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:32.160
But they don't stuff
their faces for parties,

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.070
or even because they're hungry.

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:35.883
They do it to survive.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:43.000
In the wild, yes, there
are actually wild hamsters,

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.628
they eat all kinds of food, leaves,

00:00:46.628 --> 00:00:48.910
shoots, veggies, and fruit.

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:50.760
What they don't consume right away,

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.080
they store in those
cheeks, which have pouches

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:56.300
that extend half way down their body

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.233
and expand like a balloon.

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:01.540
Thank goodness we don't
have anything like that,

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:04.193
because it would probably
look a little strange.

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:07.940
But hamsters need to stuff their faces

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:10.520
no matter how goofy it might look.

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:13.790
In fact, they have to eat
around every two hours

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:18.290
to function normally, but
foraging for food this frequently

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:20.570
would make them easy prey.

00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:23.840
Instead, they collect food at night,

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:27.103
and what they don't store,
they snack on along the way.

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:30.960
So during the day they
can hide from predators

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:33.800
and munch on their hoard in safety.

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:35.970
And thanks to the pouches in their cheeks,

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:39.440
that stockpile can get enormous.

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:40.930
Hamster burrows have been found

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:44.253
with nearly 200 pounds of stored food.

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:48.960
These cheeks also come with
special retractor muscles

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:52.323
that help the hamster stuff
itself to maximum capacity.

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:56.300
If you ever watch this
in action, you may notice

00:01:56.300 --> 00:02:00.033
that it reorients the food
after plopping it in its mouth.

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:04.240
What it's actually doing is
angling the food so it easily

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:06.963
slips to the back of the
pouch as more comes in.

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:09.980
Once the food is well on its way,

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:13.080
that's when the retractor
muscles come into play.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:16.420
When the pouch stretches,
the muscles contract,

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:19.060
which pushes the food toward the back,

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:21.610
preventing it from clogging up.

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:23.293
Pretty impressive stuff.

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:26.520
But that's not as impressive
as some of the other things

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:28.820
hamsters can do with their cheeks.

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:31.830
For starters, some species
will hide their babies

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:34.113
inside these pouches to keep them safe.

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:37.830
There are reports that others
can inflate their pouches

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:42.440
with air and use it as a
flotation device for swimming.

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:44.870
But don't try this at home.

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:47.720
Only certain wild species do this,

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:50.253
and we don't want you to
drown your poor hamster.

00:02:51.208 --> 00:02:52.760
We'd rather have you sit

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:55.393
and enjoy the incredible
cuteness of Soda Pop.

00:02:58.250 --> 00:02:59.920
Here's a fun fact.

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:03.563
Hamsters can run over five
miles in a 24-hour period.

00:03:04.683 --> 00:03:07.350
(gentle music)

